0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-WORLD-SHIELD","name":"The Shield of Achilles — Full 5-Fold Concentric Worldtext (Iliad 18.478–608)","zone":"ALL","lines":"18.478–608","greek":"Πρῶτα μὲν σάκος ποίει μέγα τε στιβαρόν τε πάντοσε δαιδάλλων... ἐν δ᾽ ἐτίθει ποταμοῖο μέγα σθένος Ὠκεανοῖο ἄντυγα πὰρ πυμάτην σάκεος πύκα ποιητοῖο.","buckley":"First of all he formed a shield, both large and solid, adorning it all over; and around it he threw a shining border, triple, glittering; and from it suspended a silver belt. Five were the folds of the shield itself... And in it he placed the vast strength of the river Oceanus, around the extreme border of the well-formed shield.","worldModel":{"vision":"84×84 stud concentric 5-fold LEGO disk uniting all five Homeric metals (Gold 297, Silver 179, Bronze 28/84, Tin 71, Kyanos 272/33) from the Cosmic Omphalos to the Oceanus Rim.","memory":"Simultaneous multi-ring state machine: polar rotation of the Bear, legal turn-taking in the Sacred Circle, river ambush escalation, golden glebe turning black behind the plough, dogs oscillating before the lions, and the Daedalean wheel/row dance.","controller":"Operative Worldtext (Bolter & Hartsoe): the viewer/warrior navigates from macro-cosmos to micro-scene, probing the rules, memory, and consequences of mortal life."}}

